157 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (This voltage is compared to whatever input the user desires. For a square wave, the duty cycle can be set with a simple voltage divider. For a sine wave, the RC circuit needs to have a high frequency \(not cutoff frequency\) to accurately PWM the signal. This also goes for triangle and sawtooth waveforms.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
