174 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (To solve this, I used a 555 timer in monostable mode, along with AND gates. When the battery is connected to the transformer, the 555 timer would start high, and after a certain length of time, say 0.5s, it would stay low until reset. But this timer should only start when the transformer needs to have current running through it, not on the disconnect. This is where the AND gate comes in. It takes the state of the Johnson counter, and decides whether or not to trigger the start on the 555 timer This start is triggered by a reset pulse from the AND gate that is connected to an RC circuit.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
